cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use ZoDAV in your work, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "ZoDAV: private Zotero WebDAV sync and zodav-audit"
authors:
  - family-names: "Rajabpour Sanati"
    given-names: "Ali"
    email: "ali@rajabpour.com"
    website: "https://rajabpour.com"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-10-01
license: AGPL-3.0-only
repository-code: "https://github.com/ali-rajabpour/ZoDAV"
url: "https://rajabpour.com"
abstract: >-
  ZoDAV is a private file-sync server for Zotero that is never on the public
  internet, reachable only over a Tailscale or Headscale network. It ships with
  zodav-audit, a standard-library Python tool that checks any Zotero WebDAV
  server for protocol conformance and file integrity, repairs what can be
  repaired safely, and raises alerts, with encrypted restic backups and a
  restore drill.
keywords:
  - zotero
  - webdav
  - self-hosted
  - tailscale
  - file-sync
  - backup
  - conformance-testing
